#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
omsid_checker.py -- Home Depot OMSID to live URL checker (single file)
======================================================================

Reads an Excel file of Home Depot OMSIDs (Internet #), checks each one against
HomeDepot.com, and writes an Excel workbook containing the live product URL or
"N/A".

HOW TO USE
----------
    1. pip install pandas openpyxl requests
    2. Put this file and your OMSID workbook in the SAME folder.
    3. Edit the SETTINGS block immediately below.
    4. Run this file (in PyCharm: right-click the editor -> Run,
       or press Ctrl+Shift+F10).

    Start with MODE = "validate". Only move on if it reports LIVE.

STATUS VALUES IN THE OUTPUT
---------------------------
    LIVE       Item resolved to a live product page; URL populated.
    NOT_FOUND  Site answered cleanly, no such item.  -> URL is "N/A"
    BLOCKED    Bot management intercepted the request. NOT a dead item.
    ERROR      Network or parse failure. NOT a dead item.
    INVALID    That input row contained no usable OMSID.

A block is never recorded as "N/A", so a throttled run cannot silently mark
live items as dead. Re-run with the same cache file to retry only the
unresolved rows.
"""

